 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Long-term Stability Analysis: Predicting PCE T80\n",
    "\n",
    "## 1. Objective\n",
    "The commercialization of perovskite solar cells is limited by their stability. This notebook analyzes the **T80 lifespan** (time until the efficiency drops to 80% of its initial value) using the project's stability dataset.\n",
    "\n",
    "## 2. Methodology\n",
    "*   **Data:** Experimental stability records from `solar_panels.parquet`.\n",
    "*   **Approach:** Log-transformation of the target variable ($T_{80}$) to handle the wide range of experimental lifespans.\n",
    "*   **Features:** Device architecture, encapsulation, and composition-dependent stress proxies."
   ],
   "id": "intro"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import joblib\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import r2_score, mean_squared_error\n",
    "\n",
    "# FORCE WHITE BACKGROUNDS\n",
    "import matplotlib as mpl\n",
    "mpl.rcParams['figure.facecolor'] = 'white'\n",
    "mpl.rcParams['axes.facecolor'] = 'white'\n",
    "mpl.rcParams['savefig.facecolor'] = 'white'\n",
    "sns.set_theme(style=\"white\", palette=\"bright\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load stability data\n",
    "df_sp = pd.read_parquet('../data/solar_panels.parquet').dropna(subset=['PCE_T80'])\n",
    "model_t80 = joblib.load('../ml_models/pce_t80_model.joblib')\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Analyzing {len(df_sp)} stability test records.\")"
   ],
   "id": "load"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Visualizing Stability Distributions\n",
    "Most perovskites fail quickly (under 100 hours), while a few high-performance candidates last over 1000 hours. This exponential distribution is best viewed on a logarithmic scale."
   ],
   "id": "dist_md"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 5), facecolor='white')\n",
    "ax = sns.histplot(df_sp['PCE_T80'], log_scale=True, kde=True, color='#e67e22')\n",
    "ax.set_facecolor(\"white\")\n",
    "plt.title(\"Distribution of Device Lifetimes (T80)\", fontsize=14)\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Hours to 80% Performance (Log Scale)\", fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ],
   "id": "dist_plot"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Stability Parity Analysis\n",
    "Comparing the predicted log-lifetimes to the actual experimental observations."
   ],
   "id": "eval_md"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Filter relevant features for the T80 model\n",
    "features = [\n",
    "    'A_1', 'A_2', 'A_3', 'B_1', 'C_1', 'C_2',\n",
    "    'en_A', 'en_B', 'en_C', 'mass_A', 'mass_B', 'mass_C',\n",
    "    'tolerance_factor', 'octahedral_factor', 'is_2d', 'dimension', 'space_group',\n",
    "    'Cell_architecture', 'ETL_stack_sequence', 'HTL_stack_sequence', 'Backcontact_stack_sequence', \n",
    "    'Stability_time_total_exposure', 'Stability_light_intensity', 'Stability_protocol', \n",
    "    'JV_default_PCE', 'Cell_area_measured', 'Perovskite_band_gap', \n",
    "    'composition_inorganic'\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "y_true_log = np.log1p(df_sp['PCE_T80'])\n",
    "y_pred_log = model_t80.predict(df_sp[features])\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(6, 6), facecolor='white')\n",
    "plt.scatter(y_true_log, y_pred_log, alpha=0.5, color='#d35400')\n",
    "plt.plot([y_true_log.min(), y_true_log.max()], [y_true_log.min(), y_true_log.max()], 'k--', lw=2)\n",
    "plt.gca().set_facecolor(\"white\")\n",
    "plt.title(f\"Log-Stability Parity Plot (R² = {r2_score(y_true_log, y_pred_log):.3f})\", fontsize=14)\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Actual log(1 + T80)\", fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Predicted log(1 + T80)\", fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ],
   "id": "parity"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Summary\n",
    "Predicting stability is significantly more challenging than predicting efficiency due to the high variability in testing conditions. However, the model correctly identifies high-stability clusters, which is essential for guiding **Inverse Design** toward durable materials."
   ],
   "id": "conclusion"
  }
 ],
